1
00:00:00,759 --> 00:00:04,759
[bright music]

2
00:00:41,689 --> 00:00:45,541
[phone rings]

3
00:00:45,583 --> 00:00:47,125
You know I'm working, right?

4
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,291
Sorry, this will be quick.

5
00:00:49,333 --> 00:00:51,625
I just need to buy some
chicken, veggies, groceries.

6
00:00:52,166 --> 00:00:55,083
Do you know where the nearest
and cheapest grocery store is?

7
00:00:55,125 --> 00:00:57,833
Emphasis on the word cheapest.

8
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:00,000
Google Maps?

9
00:01:00,708 --> 00:01:01,583
Oh, okay.

10
00:01:01,625 --> 00:01:04,250
Google Map –

11
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:07,791
Come on, I know where
the nearest grocery store is.

12
00:01:07,833 --> 00:01:10,249
What I don’t know is which
one is the most affordable.

13
00:01:10,291 --> 00:01:12,416
You know my budget is kind of limited.

14
00:01:13,083 --> 00:01:14,416
Super Mart?

15
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:17,750
Super Mart. Okay, thanks.

16
00:01:18,041 --> 00:01:19,708
- Is that all? - Yeap.

17
00:01:21,125 --> 00:01:23,875
Well, actually don’t eat dinner tonight.

18
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:25,583
I’m cooking.

19
00:01:27,250 --> 00:01:29,208
What makes you so sure
I'll eat what you'll cook?

20
00:01:29,916 --> 00:01:34,250
I just wanted to thank you for cooking
the best meal I had since I got to LA.

21
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:36,125
Okay, it wasn’t…

22
00:01:37,125 --> 00:01:39,499
You were very hungry

23
00:01:39,541 --> 00:01:42,666
and you hadn’t had
anything better in a while.

24
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,958
Well, you still didn’t have
to go through all the trouble.

25
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:52,000
It’s only because you got hurt because
I got you that gig at the liquor store.

26
00:01:52,134 --> 00:01:53,958
[playful music]

27
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,416
So you only did that out of guilt?

28
00:01:55,458 --> 00:01:57,958
That’s the only reason you were nice to me?

29
00:01:58,416 --> 00:02:00,750
I thought this was gonna be a short call?

30
00:02:01,958 --> 00:02:04,125
Okay. Well, I’m...

31
00:02:06,041 --> 00:02:06,958
Hello?

32
00:02:10,041 --> 00:02:12,416
Well, nice talking to you too.

33
00:02:13,291 --> 00:02:14,666
Bye, Josh.

34
00:02:24,862 --> 00:02:28,862
[playful music]

35
00:02:32,291 --> 00:02:34,208
Shit, that’s my bus.

36
00:02:38,458 --> 00:02:40,125
45 minutes?

37
00:02:42,166 --> 00:02:44,125
Why is there no tricycle here?

38
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,791
It’s good for the heart.

39
00:02:50,375 --> 00:02:51,625
It’s good for the heart.

40
00:02:51,958 --> 00:02:53,541
It’s good for the heart.

41
00:02:54,916 --> 00:02:57,208
It’s good for the heart.

42
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:59,250
Why is it so hot here?

43
00:02:59,666 --> 00:03:01,666
I thought it’s always cold in the US.

44
00:03:08,666 --> 00:03:09,833
Hey, sir.

45
00:03:10,375 --> 00:03:11,374
Sir!

46
00:03:11,416 --> 00:03:12,458
Sir!

47
00:03:13,416 --> 00:03:14,416
Hey.

48
00:03:14,458 --> 00:03:16,124
Do I… Do I look familiar?

49
00:03:16,166 --> 00:03:19,166
- What the fuck? - Do I look familiar?

50
00:03:19,416 --> 00:03:21,541
Get out of my way.

51
00:03:26,823 --> 00:03:30,823
[street noise]

52
00:03:59,166 --> 00:04:01,000
God, I’m starving.

53
00:04:01,791 --> 00:04:02,875
Where is he?

54
00:04:03,335 --> 00:04:05,666
[bright music]

55
00:04:05,708 --> 00:04:07,083
Surprise!

56
00:04:07,125 --> 00:04:08,333
What the?

57
00:04:08,375 --> 00:04:09,583
What are you doing?

58
00:04:09,625 --> 00:04:11,083
Heard you were looking for me.

59
00:04:11,208 --> 00:04:12,416
Miss me much?

60
00:04:12,708 --> 00:04:13,958
I don’t miss you.

61
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:17,374
I’m starving and you said
you’d take care of dinner.

62
00:04:17,416 --> 00:04:20,791
But I guess you didn’t so
I’ll heat up some leftovers.

63
00:04:20,833 --> 00:04:22,500
Who said I didn’t take care of dinner?

64
00:04:22,666 --> 00:04:23,833
What’s that?

65
00:04:24,791 --> 00:04:25,791
Jollibee.

66
00:04:26,125 --> 00:04:27,749
What’s Jollibee?

67
00:04:27,791 --> 00:04:29,833
Oh, don’t tell me you
haven’t heard of Jollibee?

68
00:04:30,125 --> 00:04:31,041
No.

69
00:04:31,083 --> 00:04:33,666
This is the most popular fast
food chain in the Philippines.

70
00:04:33,958 --> 00:04:36,708
Okay. So are we ginna eat together?

71
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:39,750
Or are you just gonna keep
endorsing your national fast food chain?

72
00:04:40,125 --> 00:04:43,999
Did you just ask if we’re
gonna eat together?

73
00:04:44,041 --> 00:04:45,500
I didn’t mean it like that.

74
00:04:47,333 --> 00:04:50,499
But it doesn’t matter anyways
because I only got one meal.

75
00:04:50,541 --> 00:04:52,625
And it’s for you.

76
00:04:56,750 --> 00:04:58,583
Oh, aren’t you gonna eat?

77
00:04:58,875 --> 00:05:00,625
You said you were starving earlier.

78
00:05:01,333 --> 00:05:02,541
I don’t wanna eat.

79
00:05:03,208 --> 00:05:03,916
Why?

80
00:05:04,625 --> 00:05:06,583
Because you’ve got nothing to eat.

81
00:05:07,041 --> 00:05:09,291
Oh, so you’re concerned about me?

82
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:11,333
Shut up.

83
00:05:11,750 --> 00:05:14,749
Don’t worry about me. I eat
Jollibee all the time in Manila.

84
00:05:14,791 --> 00:05:16,333
This one’s for you.

85
00:05:18,916 --> 00:05:21,750
Come on. Go ahead and eat it.

86
00:05:22,875 --> 00:05:23,791
Fine.

87
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:28,208
I think you’re gonna like it.

88
00:05:29,250 --> 00:05:31,458
And you probably won’t admit it.

89
00:05:31,916 --> 00:05:33,583
Because that’s kind of what you do.

90
00:05:39,083 --> 00:05:40,333
Where are you going?

91
00:05:42,630 --> 00:05:46,630
[bright music]

92
00:05:49,958 --> 00:05:51,208
There.

93
00:05:52,166 --> 00:05:53,791
- But... - Hep, hep, hep...

94
00:05:54,291 --> 00:05:55,291
just eat.

95
00:06:00,875 --> 00:06:03,000
So...

96
00:06:03,291 --> 00:06:07,375
does that mean that this
is officially our first date?

97
00:06:09,541 --> 00:06:11,166
What are you talking about?

98
00:06:11,208 --> 00:06:14,874
This. Us. Eating together.

99
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:17,374
No, this is not a date.

100
00:06:17,416 --> 00:06:23,291
This is me not wanting to eat
alone and have you look at me.

101
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:24,541
Mmm...

102
00:06:24,583 --> 00:06:27,541
But I always look at you.

103
00:06:32,458 --> 00:06:33,874
Will you stop being so…

104
00:06:33,916 --> 00:06:34,833
So…

105
00:06:34,875 --> 00:06:35,749
sweet? Charming? Lovable?

106
00:06:35,791 --> 00:06:36,666
Charming?

107
00:06:36,708 --> 00:06:38,208
Lovable?

108
00:06:38,375 --> 00:06:40,250
I was gonna say insufferable.

109
00:06:47,166 --> 00:06:49,625
What happened to your plan, by the way?

110
00:06:49,958 --> 00:06:52,166
What plan?

111
00:06:52,625 --> 00:06:58,333
Your plan to go out and buy
some rice and veggies and chicken,

112
00:06:58,375 --> 00:07:00,666
and cook some Filipino food?

113
00:07:00,916 --> 00:07:03,583
Oh, yeah. No, um…

114
00:07:03,625 --> 00:07:07,833
Nothing happened. I just
thought this would be better.

115
00:07:11,666 --> 00:07:16,958
You know, you can’t cover everything
up with this everything’s okay attitude.

116
00:07:17,875 --> 00:07:19,041
You can tell me.

117
00:07:19,208 --> 00:07:20,291
What happened?

118
00:07:20,875 --> 00:07:21,749
Nothing happened.

119
00:07:21,791 --> 00:07:23,625
Um, I just...

120
00:07:23,750 --> 00:07:24,500
um,

121
00:07:25,208 --> 00:07:26,750
thought this would be better.

122
00:07:29,291 --> 00:07:30,833
I hate you for being a liar.

123
00:07:31,250 --> 00:07:32,416
I'm not a liar.

124
00:07:32,458 --> 00:07:33,375
Really?

125
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:39,166
Give me an update about
your Hollywood project then.

126
00:07:40,125 --> 00:07:42,708
Oh, um, that…

127
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:43,833
Yeah, no, um,

128
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:46,708
it’s going, uh, great!

129
00:07:46,750 --> 00:07:49,083
We already started treatment on the script.

130
00:07:49,583 --> 00:07:50,208
Wow.

131
00:07:50,583 --> 00:07:51,583
What’s it about?

132
00:07:51,750 --> 00:07:53,583
What’s it about? Um,

133
00:07:53,791 --> 00:07:55,083
Yeah, no, it's um,

134
00:07:55,125 --> 00:07:56,541
The story is about…

135
00:07:57,208 --> 00:07:58,583
It’s about

136
00:07:59,541 --> 00:08:01,958
um, something I can’t talk about.

137
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:04,416
Because we have
confidentiality agreements, NDAs.

138
00:08:04,458 --> 00:08:05,584
Got it.

139
00:08:05,626 --> 00:08:07,791
[bright music]

140
00:08:07,833 --> 00:08:11,083
By the way, there’s a job opening
at the liquor store, if you want it.

141
00:08:11,958 --> 00:08:14,166
One of the other crew members resigned.

142
00:08:14,666 --> 00:08:15,833
Oh, why?

143
00:08:16,666 --> 00:08:17,624
I don’t know.

144
00:08:17,666 --> 00:08:20,041
Could it have anything to
do with unfair labor practices?

145
00:08:20,083 --> 00:08:22,249
I don’t know where this is
going. Do you want the job or not?

146
00:08:22,291 --> 00:08:24,833
- No, yeah, yeah.
- Okay, because you seem more interested

147
00:08:24,875 --> 00:08:26,958
in why this other crew member resigned.

148
00:08:28,291 --> 00:08:29,208
I’m a writer.

149
00:08:29,250 --> 00:08:31,208
I’m always more
interested in the backstory.

150
00:08:32,083 --> 00:08:32,749
Okay.

151
00:08:32,791 --> 00:08:35,166
Well, if you want, you can start tomorrow,

152
00:08:35,208 --> 00:08:37,666
5pm – 10pm.

153
00:08:37,875 --> 00:08:39,208
70 bucks.

154
00:08:39,833 --> 00:08:43,125
70 bucks for 5 hours.

155
00:08:47,791 --> 00:08:49,291
3,500 pesos?

156
00:08:49,916 --> 00:08:52,083
I don’t know US dollars to pesos.

157
00:08:52,375 --> 00:08:53,708
I wanna hug you right now.

158
00:08:53,791 --> 00:08:55,125
Please don’t.

159
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:59,250
I think deep down inside,
some part of you likes me.

160
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:02,000
No, not even a little.

161
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:05,208
Right. So who’s lying now?

162
00:09:07,791 --> 00:09:10,041
I had an opening for a job.

163
00:09:10,541 --> 00:09:12,208
You’ve said you needed a job.

164
00:09:12,250 --> 00:09:13,708
I offered you the job.

165
00:09:13,750 --> 00:09:15,458
And you accepted the job.

166
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:17,791
I don’t know what about
that implies that I like you.

167
00:09:18,583 --> 00:09:22,666
Maybe the part where you just
can’t help but do a few things for me.

168
00:09:23,208 --> 00:09:25,458
You know, sometimes
it’s not what people say.

169
00:09:25,708 --> 00:09:27,541
Sometimes it’s what they do.

170
00:09:29,122 --> 00:09:33,122
[bright music]

171
00:09:39,416 --> 00:09:40,083
What?

172
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:41,291
No comeback?

173
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:45,833
You’re a writer.

174
00:09:46,166 --> 00:09:47,666
I don’t argue with writers.

175
00:09:47,708 --> 00:09:51,750
You have a response plotted out in
your head. I can’t compete with that.

176
00:09:54,583 --> 00:09:56,416
I’m just gonna enjoy this moment.

177
00:09:57,291 --> 00:09:59,958
Eating Jollibee for the first time, I mean.

178
00:10:00,833 --> 00:10:02,041
And you’re right.

179
00:10:02,333 --> 00:10:03,416
It’s very good.

180
00:10:05,885 --> 00:10:09,885
[bright music]

181
00:10:14,625 --> 00:10:16,374
Really, bestfriend?

182
00:10:16,416 --> 00:10:18,124
He pushed you?

183
00:10:18,166 --> 00:10:19,833
That's sad.

184
00:10:20,458 --> 00:10:21,791
I know, right?

185
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:23,874
I mean, he could've just easily ran away.

186
00:10:23,916 --> 00:10:26,666
But to push your son who
you saw for the first time?

187
00:10:27,541 --> 00:10:30,249
But are you sure that he's your dad?

188
00:10:30,291 --> 00:10:31,999
What if he just looks like him?

189
00:10:32,041 --> 00:10:34,958
It already happened before, remember?

190
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,333
You have mistaken someone else as your dad.

191
00:10:38,375 --> 00:10:41,333
And now, you're in America.

192
00:10:41,375 --> 00:10:44,875
A lot more people look like your dad.

193
00:10:45,666 --> 00:10:47,416
I don't know, bestfriend.

194
00:10:47,458 --> 00:10:48,833
But wait bestfriend...

195
00:10:48,875 --> 00:10:50,416
why are you like that?

196
00:10:50,458 --> 00:10:51,583
What do you mean?

197
00:10:51,625 --> 00:10:54,958
You just saw someone who
you thought was your father.

198
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:58,416
Then he pushed you to the
ground and told you to go away.

199
00:10:58,458 --> 00:10:59,833
So?

200
00:10:59,875 --> 00:11:04,000
Shouldn’t you be sad and miserable?

201
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:07,625
You've been looking for him since birth.

202
00:11:07,916 --> 00:11:11,249
But why do you seem so happy?

203
00:11:11,291 --> 00:11:13,875
You're blooming!

204
00:11:14,541 --> 00:11:16,291
I just don't want to
waste my time and energy

205
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:18,416
thinking about people who don't want me.

206
00:11:18,458 --> 00:11:21,041
He left me and my mom,

207
00:11:21,083 --> 00:11:23,499
abandoned us as if we meant nothing.

208
00:11:23,541 --> 00:11:26,250
If he doesn’t want to accept me,

209
00:11:26,625 --> 00:11:27,541
that's fine.

210
00:11:27,583 --> 00:11:29,375
It’s his loss, not mine.

211
00:11:30,041 --> 00:11:32,958
It doesn’t feel that way, bestfriend.

212
00:11:33,416 --> 00:11:35,000
Tell me what you think then.

213
00:11:35,666 --> 00:11:38,000
You’re in love!

214
00:11:41,250 --> 00:11:42,375
I knew it!

215
00:11:42,958 --> 00:11:44,291
My instincts never fail me!

216
00:11:44,750 --> 00:11:46,875
You've already found someone new!

217
00:11:47,333 --> 00:11:49,249
Just less than a month in America

218
00:11:49,291 --> 00:11:51,291
and you're already flirting!

219
00:11:51,708 --> 00:11:53,624
Bestfriend,

220
00:11:53,666 --> 00:11:56,708
You know you're my one and only.

221
00:11:56,833 --> 00:12:01,625
Even if I met the most important,
amazing person in the world,

222
00:12:01,916 --> 00:12:04,541
no one could ever replace you in my heart.

223
00:12:05,416 --> 00:12:07,291
That's so romantic!

224
00:12:07,333 --> 00:12:08,541
Happy now?

225
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:17,600
[bright music]

226
00:12:19,375 --> 00:12:20,833
Oh, what happened?

227
00:12:22,875 --> 00:12:24,000
Turn it off.

228
00:12:24,333 --> 00:12:25,416
I'm sleeping.

229
00:12:26,625 --> 00:12:27,225
Oh.

230
00:12:27,416 --> 00:12:28,083
Sorry.

231
00:12:44,708 --> 00:12:47,458
Hey, what time am I supposed
to report to work tomorrow?

232
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:51,208
Hey, um, what part of I'm
sleeping don't you understand?

233
00:12:52,458 --> 00:12:54,083
Sorry, Josh.

234
00:12:55,708 --> 00:12:59,166
And what part of "don't call
me Josh" don't you understand?

235
00:13:00,666 --> 00:13:03,416
What's wrong? We were
just having a good time earlier.

236
00:13:03,458 --> 00:13:06,541
- We’re being really sweet
and – - I wasn’t being sweet.

237
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:08,791
But you were.

238
00:13:10,208 --> 00:13:13,000
How many times do I have to tell you?

239
00:13:13,541 --> 00:13:15,708
I was looking for a replacement
crew member at work.

240
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:18,374
And it just so happened that
you were also looking for a job.

241
00:13:18,416 --> 00:13:19,500
Okay? That’s it.

242
00:13:20,375 --> 00:13:22,458
Stop making a big deal of it.

243
00:13:23,125 --> 00:13:27,708
Says the guy who was just
splitting his meal into half for me

244
00:13:28,458 --> 00:13:30,916
and seemed kind of sweet to me.

245
00:13:31,666 --> 00:13:33,458
I didn’t want to eat your food

246
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:35,166
and you need more money than I do.

247
00:13:35,208 --> 00:13:37,625
You couldn’t even
afford two Jollibee meals.

248
00:13:40,333 --> 00:13:41,666
So that’s it?

249
00:13:43,458 --> 00:13:44,791
Just like that.

250
00:13:46,291 --> 00:13:49,583
We're back to the beginning
and it’s just all about money?

251
00:13:51,791 --> 00:13:53,833
It’s always just been about the money.

252
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:56,083
You’re not part of my life.

253
00:13:56,708 --> 00:13:59,666
Give me 300 or you’re out in three days.

254
00:14:10,875 --> 00:14:12,375
Hey, what are you doing?

255
00:14:13,708 --> 00:14:14,666
Hey!

256
00:14:16,291 --> 00:14:17,625
Where are you going?

257
00:14:22,283 --> 00:14:26,283
[street noise]

258
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:32,430
[soft music]

259
00:14:47,583 --> 00:14:49,416
Answer the phone please...

260
00:14:57,916 --> 00:15:00,041
Hey, where the hell are you?

261
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:05,416
I’m fine. Don’t worry about me.

262
00:15:06,958 --> 00:15:09,833
It’s three in the morning
and it’s not safe out there.

263
00:15:11,958 --> 00:15:13,708
I can take care of myself.

264
00:15:16,666 --> 00:15:18,416
Look, we both have to go to sleep.

265
00:15:18,458 --> 00:15:21,291
Just come back. We’ll talk
about this in the morning.

266
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:26,791
Don’t worry.

267
00:15:28,208 --> 00:15:30,541
I’ll get you the rest of your rent money.

268
00:15:34,958 --> 00:15:38,749
Okay look, I’m sorry for everything I said.

269
00:15:38,791 --> 00:15:42,541
I am sorry that I hurt you.

270
00:15:47,166 --> 00:15:48,916
Please just come back.

271
00:15:49,208 --> 00:15:52,791
I’m really sorry. I’m really
fucking worried about you.

272
00:15:55,708 --> 00:15:58,291
I’ll come pick you up. Where are you?

273
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:09,750
[soft music]

274
00:16:17,791 --> 00:16:18,791
Thanks.

275
00:16:20,083 --> 00:16:21,291
Are you okay?

276
00:16:26,375 --> 00:16:28,416
You know, even if you're mad,

277
00:16:28,458 --> 00:16:31,749
you shouldn't go out there
in the middle of the night.

278
00:16:31,791 --> 00:16:34,041
- It's not safe— - I saw him.

279
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:35,625
Who?

280
00:16:37,958 --> 00:16:39,625
I saw my father.

281
00:16:40,375 --> 00:16:42,375
Or someone who looks like him. I don't...

282
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,166
I don't know.

283
00:16:46,083 --> 00:16:48,500
I was walking back from the groceries

284
00:16:49,833 --> 00:16:51,541
when I just spotted him.

285
00:16:54,291 --> 00:16:57,083
My mom met my dad when he
was stationed in the Philippines.

286
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:01,416
He was in the U.S. Navy,

287
00:17:02,208 --> 00:17:03,500
I think.

288
00:17:05,166 --> 00:17:07,708
But he left us right after I was born.

289
00:17:10,333 --> 00:17:15,333
My mom says there was a
volcanic eruption in our province.

290
00:17:15,708 --> 00:17:18,250
And all the US troops had to be pulled out.

291
00:17:21,416 --> 00:17:23,166
That's why I never met him.

292
00:17:26,416 --> 00:17:28,458
So I always grew up wondering

293
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:31,250
what it was like to have a father,

294
00:17:32,833 --> 00:17:34,708
just like any other kid.

295
00:17:36,916 --> 00:17:39,291
My mom said never to look for him,

296
00:17:40,291 --> 00:17:41,958
not to bother.

297
00:17:42,507 --> 00:17:43,583
[soft music]

298
00:17:43,625 --> 00:17:45,541
But you know me,

299
00:17:46,166 --> 00:17:47,666
I'm stubborn.

300
00:17:48,750 --> 00:17:50,416
So a couple of years ago,

301
00:17:50,458 --> 00:17:54,749
I asked a friend of mine
who lived here in the US

302
00:17:54,791 --> 00:17:56,625
to help me with my father.

303
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,500
And I don't know how he did it, but

304
00:17:59,625 --> 00:18:02,583
he found out a lot about him.

305
00:18:02,916 --> 00:18:07,458
His email, pictures,

306
00:18:07,916 --> 00:18:11,458
his home address, Facebook accounts.

307
00:18:11,833 --> 00:18:14,916
It’s kind of funny because
he had like ten of them.

308
00:18:17,291 --> 00:18:19,875
I was so excited back then

309
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:22,291
because I thought this is it.

310
00:18:23,250 --> 00:18:25,291
I’m finally gonna meet my father.

311
00:18:28,750 --> 00:18:31,916
So like the next day, I emailed him.

312
00:18:32,666 --> 00:18:36,041
I messaged all his Facebook accounts.

313
00:18:38,333 --> 00:18:39,875
But you know what he did?

314
00:18:41,583 --> 00:18:43,666
He deactivated all his Facebook accounts,

315
00:18:43,708 --> 00:18:45,708
the email I sent bounced.

316
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,416
He couldn’t bother to say

317
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,208
“Hey, um, it’s me.

318
00:18:52,250 --> 00:18:53,958
It’s nice to meet you son.

319
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:57,375
I’m sorry things turned out
the way they did. But, uh,

320
00:18:58,541 --> 00:19:03,333
you know, I got a wife and kids
and I don’t want you to ruin that.”

321
00:19:03,884 --> 00:19:07,583
[dramatic music]

322
00:19:07,625 --> 00:19:12,541
Because at least that would
have been an acknowledgment.

323
00:19:13,791 --> 00:19:16,541
At least that would have been an
acknowledgment that I’m his son.

324
00:19:20,291 --> 00:19:22,416
That’s all I wanted from him.

325
00:19:23,291 --> 00:19:25,374
Because I don’t need anything from him.

326
00:19:25,416 --> 00:19:27,083
I don’t need money from him.

327
00:19:27,125 --> 00:19:29,583
My mom’s worked hard her entire life

328
00:19:30,375 --> 00:19:32,833
so she could give us everything we needed.

329
00:19:36,666 --> 00:19:38,083
I’m just…

330
00:19:38,291 --> 00:19:41,375
I’m just starting to sound
crazy and desperate.

331
00:19:43,708 --> 00:19:46,166
You know, because deep down inside I know…

332
00:19:47,416 --> 00:19:49,375
He doesn’t want me.

333
00:19:49,833 --> 00:19:52,208
He doesn’t care about me.

334
00:19:54,458 --> 00:19:58,291
And I’m never gonna see him.

335
00:20:05,344 --> 00:20:09,344
[dramatic music]

336
00:20:54,875 --> 00:20:57,999
- Good morning. - Good morning.

337
00:20:58,041 --> 00:20:59,749
Did you want me to help you with that?

338
00:20:59,791 --> 00:21:03,333
No, I’m good. You can
make some coffee if you want.

339
00:21:03,625 --> 00:21:06,041
Okay. Did you want me to make you some?

340
00:21:06,083 --> 00:21:09,083
No, I’m good. I don’t drink coffee.

341
00:21:09,333 --> 00:21:14,458
You are the first person I’ve
ever met who doesn’t drink coffee.

342
00:21:23,682 --> 00:21:27,682
[bright music]

343
00:21:35,166 --> 00:21:36,749
This is really good.

344
00:21:36,791 --> 00:21:38,333
Thank you!

345
00:21:40,750 --> 00:21:43,000
You know, you should start a food business.

346
00:21:43,375 --> 00:21:47,458
Yeah, like Korean food. Samgyupsal.

347
00:21:47,916 --> 00:21:50,583
You won’t even start with
something big like a restaurant.

348
00:21:50,625 --> 00:21:54,541
You could just do like
online orders, food deliveries.

349
00:21:54,916 --> 00:21:56,916
Oh, maybe even a food truck!

350
00:21:56,958 --> 00:21:59,749
I don’t want to do that.

351
00:21:59,791 --> 00:22:02,625
This is egg and bread.

352
00:22:03,458 --> 00:22:07,374
Okay, but one day, you’re
gonna look back at this moment

353
00:22:07,416 --> 00:22:12,041
and you’re gonna think I really
should have listened to that Andre.

354
00:22:12,083 --> 00:22:16,791
As for me, I’m gonna miss your
cooking when I go back to the Philippines.

355
00:22:18,291 --> 00:22:20,791
Isn’t there Korean food there?

356
00:22:20,916 --> 00:22:24,541
Yeah, but you know,
it’s different without...

357
00:22:29,041 --> 00:22:32,708
Actually, um, can I ask you something?

358
00:22:32,750 --> 00:22:34,083
Yeah, sure.

359
00:22:34,375 --> 00:22:36,291
Promise you’re not gonna get mad?

360
00:22:37,291 --> 00:22:39,875
Depends on the question.

361
00:22:40,291 --> 00:22:43,625
Um, never mind.

362
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:47,708
You can’t do that. You can’t start
asking question and then say never mind.

363
00:22:48,250 --> 00:22:50,416
Then promise me you’re not gonna get mad.

364
00:22:51,083 --> 00:22:53,125
Fine, I promise.

365
00:22:54,250 --> 00:22:57,583
What happened with you last night?

366
00:22:58,625 --> 00:23:01,458
What do you mean what
happened with me last night?

367
00:23:02,250 --> 00:23:05,916
We’re having a nice night, sharing a meal.

368
00:23:05,958 --> 00:23:09,749
And then I went to CR.

369
00:23:09,791 --> 00:23:10,999
The CR?

370
00:23:11,041 --> 00:23:14,958
Uh, yeah, that's what we call it,
CR. Stands for Comfort Room.

371
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,125
Oh, the bathroom.

372
00:23:17,708 --> 00:23:18,583
Um, yeah.

373
00:23:18,625 --> 00:23:20,458
So I went to the CR,

374
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:22,541
or uh, bathroom.

375
00:23:22,583 --> 00:23:25,499
And when I got back, you were mad.

376
00:23:25,541 --> 00:23:27,624
Yeah, um…

377
00:23:27,666 --> 00:23:31,624
I told you to never make
phone calls in the bathroom.

378
00:23:31,666 --> 00:23:33,291
What if I need to pee?

379
00:23:34,333 --> 00:23:37,166
That’s it? That’s why you were mad?

380
00:23:40,375 --> 00:23:42,208
Oh, okay.

381
00:23:43,333 --> 00:23:45,125
You could have just knocked.

382
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,666
You know what,

383
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:52,874
I promise I will never again
take a phone call from in the toilet.

384
00:23:52,916 --> 00:23:55,416
- In the toilet? - In the bathroom.

385
00:23:58,713 --> 00:24:02,713
[bright music]

386
00:24:16,916 --> 00:24:19,458
Hey, can I ask you something too?

387
00:24:20,541 --> 00:24:23,208
Yeah, you can ask me anything.

388
00:24:23,708 --> 00:24:28,749
I know it’s none of my business
but that’s your partner, right?

389
00:24:28,791 --> 00:24:29,749
Huh?

390
00:24:29,791 --> 00:24:32,541
Lover, significant other, special someone?

391
00:24:32,583 --> 00:24:35,833
The person you were talking
to on the phone last night.

392
00:24:35,875 --> 00:24:37,208
I’m not following.

393
00:24:37,250 --> 00:24:39,708
You can tell me. It’s okay.

394
00:24:41,291 --> 00:24:45,291
Well, I’m not in a relationship.

395
00:24:45,333 --> 00:24:49,666
But if you’re asking who I
was talking to last night, uh...

396
00:24:50,041 --> 00:24:52,791
Oh yeah, I was talking to my bestfriend.

397
00:24:53,416 --> 00:24:57,541
A lot of people sometimes think we’re
together because we call each other “besh”

398
00:24:57,583 --> 00:24:59,916
and we’re so ridiculous but...

399
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:03,291
Wait.

400
00:25:04,166 --> 00:25:06,374
Is that why you got mad last night?

401
00:25:06,416 --> 00:25:08,250
What? No!

402
00:25:09,458 --> 00:25:10,958
You were jealous!

403
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,833
Stop it. I wasn’t.

404
00:25:16,250 --> 00:25:21,541
- You were jealous!
- No, no! I told you I wasn’t jealous.

405
00:25:21,875 --> 00:25:24,291
You don’t have to worry about “besh”.

406
00:25:24,875 --> 00:25:27,666
You know what, I’m
gonna introduce you to her.

407
00:25:27,708 --> 00:25:29,624
You don’t have to do that.

408
00:25:29,666 --> 00:25:31,041
I want to.

409
00:25:31,083 --> 00:25:34,333
I want her to know who’s
making me smile while I’m here.

410
00:25:34,375 --> 00:25:37,416
Even if my luck has
otherwise run out in LA.

411
00:25:42,160 --> 00:25:46,160
[bright music]

412
00:26:26,427 --> 00:26:30,427
[bright music]

413
00:27:16,424 --> 00:27:20,424
[bright music]
